To override a block of the storefront header logo template in your plugin, you need to extend from the original `logo.html.twig` file and replace its contents with your custom content. Here's how you can do it:

```twig [PLUGIN_ROOT/src/Resources/views/storefront/layout/header/logo.html.twig]
{% sw_extends '@Storefront/storefront/layout/header/logo.html.twig' %}

{% block layout_header_logo_link %}
    <h2>Hello world!</h2>
{% endblock %}
```

This code snippet extends from the original `logo.html.twig` file and overrides the `layout_header_logo_link` block with your custom text. If you want to append your text to the logo instead of replacing it, you could add a line like this: <code v-pre>{{ parent() }}</code>

Remember to clear the cache and refresh your storefront after making these changes.

