To override Bootstrap SCSS variables like `$border-radius`, you need to create a `overrides.scss` file in your theme's SCSS entry point, which is defined in the `theme.json`. Here’s how you can do it:

```javascript
// <plugin root>/src/Resources/theme.json
{
  "name": "SwagBasicExampleTheme",
  "author": "Shopware AG",
  "views": [
        "@Storefront",
        "@Plugins"
    ],
  "style": [
    "app/storefront/src/scss/overrides.scss", <-- Variable overrides
    "@Storefront",
    "app/storefront/src/scss/base.scss"
  ],
  "script": [
    "@Storefront",
    "app/storefront/dist/storefront/js/just-another-theme/just-another-theme.js"
  ],
  "asset": [
    "@Storefront",
    "app/storefront/src/assets"
  ]
}
```

In the `overrides.scss` file, you can override default Bootstrap variables like this:

```css
// <plugin root>/src/Resources/app/storefront/src/scss/overrides.scss
$border-radius: 0;

// some other override examples
$icon-base-color: #f00;
$modal-backdrop-bg: rgba(255, 0, 0, 0.5);
$disabled-btn-bg: #f00;
$disabled-btn-border-color: #fc8;
$font-weight-semibold: 300;
```

After saving the `overrides.scss` file and running `bin/console theme:compile`, you can check out the Storefront in the browser to see if the changes have been applied. The `$border-radius` should be removed for every element.

